-  "$comment": "FROZEN SEAMS \u2014 mission-start audit (s113-m01, Rule 1). These 5 integration seams are frozen NOW so m02/m03/m04 add code, not schema churn. (a) CROSS-PANEL DATA-SHARING: shared dataset-level rows at `datasets[]`; panels reference a dataset by `datasetId` + field refs in `encodings` \u2014 NOT inline-rows-per-panel, which bloats payload AND blocks cross-filter (tabular panels must share a dimensional space). Non-tabular branches (hierarchy/sankey/network/geo) are structurally distinct and carried inline on the panel. (b) PARTIAL-PANEL ERROR policy: `onPanelError` default 'placeholder' \u2014 render an a11y-described error panel in-place, don't void the whole dashboard. (c) CROSS-SOURCE LINK combination: `crossFilter` default { combine:'and', ignoreSelfSource:true } \u2014 each active source ANDs a predicate; a panel ignores its OWN source selection; per-link override via `links[].combine`. (d) DASHBOARD-LEVEL A11Y: `a11y` (required) carries a cross-panel summary + `readingOrder` default 'kpi-first' (KPI row read/focused before charts); the per-chart AccessibilitySpec stays per-panel. (e) TOKEN strategy: one dashboard-level `tokenCssRef` (deferred to the consumer CSS bundle per viz.render's compact/tokenCssRef posture); KPI threshold metadata is SEMANTIC only (`threshold.direction`/`value`) \u2014 colors do NOT resolve inline. ALSO frozen in m01 (as hand-authored TS, not this schema, since they are runtime interaction state not declarative config): the Selection / SelectionState types in packages/viz-core/src/spec/dashboard-selection.ts, so m03 (cross-filter resolver) and m04 (linked-selection reducer) depend ONLY on m01. The links predicate vocabulary reuses the SectionFilter operator grammar (==|!=|in|not_in|>|>=|<|<=). DEFERRED: brush/interval RANGE selections (point/categorical only v1); anomaly narration (threshold/outlier flag only); the general composer (fixed template first). DOWNSTREAM CONTRACT CLARIFICATIONS (frozen so m02-m05 add code, not schema): (i) KPI TIME AXIS \u2014 the KPI sparkline, comparison.basis 'window', and aggregate 'latest' ALL read DATASET ROW ORDER as the time axis (rows arrive pre-ordered from the producer); there is no separate KPI period/time field in v1 (an explicit period axis would be a v0.2 additive field \u2014 the most likely future churn point). (ii) CROSS-FILTER SOURCE DIMENSION \u2014 DashboardLink.sourceField defaults to the source panel's primary dimension = a TABULAR panel's encodings.x field; a non-tabular source panel (hierarchy/sankey/network/geo) has no encodings block and MUST set links[].sourceField explicitly, else it is not a valid v1 cross-filter source. (iii) SELECTION VALUES \u2014 cross-filter Selection.values are string|number ONLY in v1 (boolean dimensions out of scope), so the m04 canonical-ordering normalizer never sorts a boolean. (iv) VENDORED COPY \u2014 packages/viz-core/src/spec/dashboard-spec.schema.json is a hand-synced byte-identical copy of this source (the validator inlines it); a viz-core parity test asserts identity, but re-copy on every edit and keep it in the s113 closeout gate sweep.",
